I finished my first ever rogue ascension today (Thursday, 1st of July).
On Sunday, the 27th of June, I looked at my logfile statistics and saw
that rogue was the character I had least played on 3.4.3.
There were only 7 rogues in my 3.4.3 Linux logfile then, the next smallest
number being 9 for A, P and Ran.
So I started another rogue, leaving the rest random, and the RNG
decided to make me an orc. (I had never ascended an orc before, either..)

I didn't use my original short sword much, I almost immediately began
wielding one of the orcish daggers I was born with, and practicing
#twoweaponing with it and another dagger whenever I felt it was safe.

On dungeon level 6, I managed to convert an originally lawful altar
to chaotic, and a few hundred turns and some #offerings later I received
Stormbringer from Kos. It remained my main weapon for the rest of the
game, only to be sometimes replaced by some dagger for safety reasons
when I was near temple priests, shopkeepers or the Minetown guards, or
my quest mentor or the peaceful @ on the Home 1 level.

Got the bag from Sokoban, and that helped a lot in carrying stuff..
The Mine end level was version 1, the original one. On that level
a mind flayer managed to surprise me and flay me once, but fortunately
I didn't lose TOO many identifications..

This time there were totally 6 random altars, 4 of them attended by
priests. And two of the attended ones were co-aligned. The unattended
ones that were originally cross-aligned, got converted..
So, there were many places to sacrifice, but Stormbringer remained the
only artifact gift I got from Kos. Not that I exactly needed anything
else.

No Bigroom level this time, and didn't find the entrance to Ludios either.

I found a spellbook of light early in the game, and noticed that rogues
aren't restricted in the divination spells, so I began practicing with
it every time I had the chance, even though I sucked in it at first,
with failure rates somewhere near 70% even when I took away all my
armor.. you guess why? Yeah, I wanted to have the divination school 
practiced in case I happen to find a spell of identify! And I did!
When I got divination practiced to the basic level, the failrate in
identify dropped from 100% to something like 52%, and it was good enough
then for a spell that wasn't needed for emergency use, I could wait until
I was alone on the whole dungeon level before casting it..

When I found the Medusa level, which was the version where Medusa is
on the East side of the level, I had no means of levitation, and the
only item that could help me with crossing the water was a single
wand of cold. I realized it didn't have enough charges to freeze the
whole route, so I collected all the rings I had left laying around the
dungeon and polypiled until I got a ring of levitation. I also got a
ring of polymorph control in the polypiling session, good for the Quest.

I was still explevel 13 when I found the Castle, and I had no magic 
resistance yet. Fortunately I had found a shield of reflection earlier.
Since I had never ascended a rogue before, I didn't care about conducts
this time, and ended up blessing one of the two scrolls of genocide I
had found earlier and genociding L before clearing the castle.
I built the tunnel of boulders around the drawbridge played the little
mastermind to get the passtune (acdeg this time, fast to figure out..)
and started killing the folks inside, occasionally using the drawbridge
guillotine for some folks I didn't want to have contact with.

In the Castle I reached explevel 14 (purely by killing, I never quaffed
a potion of gain level or ate wraith corpses), and since none of the 
dragons inside was gray, I gave up another conduct and wished for a
gray dragon scale mail (got it at +0).

In the Quest there were many nagas of various kinds on the first filler
level, and they wore me down with their paralyzation attacks.. I grabbed
the wand of wishing and wished for a ring of free action (hadn't found one
yet and didn't get one from the polypiling), but got beaten down by the N
bunch before I could put it on. Luckily I was wearing an amulet of life
saving. (Of course I later saw SEVERAL more rings of free action in
Gehennom and took another one of them with me just in case..)
After I had mapped out the quest filler levels and the locate level and 
the part of the goal level that was accessible normally, I returned to
the first filler level where I had earlier found a polymorph trap.
Took of my cloak, GDSM and shirt, put on my ring of polymorph control,
stepped into the trap and became a xorn.
When I had caught the attention of Master Assassin, I returned to my 
orcish form before getting out of that part of the level, but there was
another polytrap there so I didn't need to zap the wand of polymorph
at me here either. Got him persuaded to give me the Key and the Bell.

Then.. down to Gehennom.
I began seeing master mind flayers here and there, so as I had already
broken the genoless conduct, I decided to genocide them as well with the
scroll I had left uncursed.
And when I was on the middle level of the Wizard's house, I decided to
write one more scroll of genocide and get rid of the regular mind flayers
as well.

After killing Rodney the first time, I realized I didn't have speed boots.
So I used one more wish for them and left my +6 elven boots behind.
I got the speed boots as +3 as I had wished, and wrote another blessed
scroll of enchant armor for them. I know it is risky to strip to just
the boots after killing Rodney, but that floor of the house was cleared
and nothing harassed me within the few turns that it took to get the
boots to +4.

The mysterious force kicked in more than I expected for a chaotic 
character: 44->44,38->38,38->38,37->38,35->36,33->33
(38 was Baalz level, and the stairs to Vlad's tower were also there.
 35 was Juiblex.)

The wizard reappeared the first time on Juiblex level, where he also double
troubled. Next appearance was on Asmodeus' level (31), next in the 
Valley (30), next on 15, then on 2 where he double troubled again,
the guaranteed one on Earth and finally once more on the Air level 
where he double troubled again.
That's totally 11 incarnations of Wizard of Yendor to be killed.

What else.. I got all scrolls identified, all potions except polymorph.
Rings of protection and gain constitution were left unseen.

On Astral level, I decided to try the middle altar first, and it was the
right one.

So, now I have ascended B, C, K, M, P, Rog, S, V, W (not all of these in
3.4.3, but in different versions since 3.3.1 which is the oldest one I
still have logfiles from).
A, H, Ran, T to go and I hadn't ascended any of these in pre-3.3.1 versions
either.

